regressions.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Establish a tiered testing convention: (1) simple skills (< 200 lines, no external deps) → manual evals acceptable, (2) medium skills (200-500 lines) → evals.json with file-existence and basic schema assertions, (3) complex skills (> 500 lines or external deps) → full pytest integration suite (see tests/cli/prd/test_e2e.py as a model). Document the convention in docs/developer-guide/testing-skills.md. For sc-auggie-review-protocol specifically, add a tests/skills/test_sc_auggie_review.py with at least 3 integration tests matching the 3 eval scenarios, with assertions that REVIEW.md exists, has the required sections, and contains no hallucinated file:line citations.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Project-local vs global hook registration pattern is underdocumented and creates drift between _FRESHNESS_SCRIPTS and actual registration\",\n      \"category\": \"architecture\",\n      \"severity_hint\": \"medium\",\n      \"affected_files\": [\n        \"src/superclaude/cli/install_hooks.py\",\n        \".claude/settings.json\",\n        \"src/superclaude/hooks/scripts/offer-pr-review.sh\",\n        \"src/superclaude/hooks/scripts/reject-workspace-writes.sh\"\n      ],\n      \"why\": \"Two hooks in the repo are project-local (reject-workspace-writes.sh, offer-pr-review.sh) — they're registered in .claude/settings.json with $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR paths, so they only run in this repo. However, both are listed in _FRESHNESS_SCRIPTS (install_hooks.py:66, :179), which copies them to ~/.claude/hooks/ on all end-user installs. The copied scripts are never registered in those users' settings.json and never run. The Makefile verify-sync check (line 308) enforces that every script in src/superclaude/hooks/scripts/ is in _FRESHNESS_SCRIPTS, but it doesn't distinguish project-local scripts. This creates confusion: the _FRESHNESS_SCRIPTS list looks like a global-install registry, but 2 of its 9 entries are actually project-local dormants.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Introduce a _PROJECT_LOCAL_SCRIPTS constant in install_hooks.py for scripts that are NOT copied to ~/.claude/hooks/ during global install. Update _copy_scripts to skip project-local scripts. Update Makefile verify-sync to exclude project-local scripts from the drift check. Document the distinction in install_hooks.py docstring: 'Scripts in _FRESHNESS_SCRIPTS are installed globally; scripts in _PROJECT_LOCAL_SCRIPTS are project-specific and registered in .claude/settings.json only.'\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Auggie CLI invocation documentation duplicates across SKILL.md and evals/, with inconsistencies in JSON extraction pipeline\",\n      \"category\": \"docs\",\n      \"severity_hint\": \"medium\",\n      \"affected_files\": [\n        \"src/superclaude/skills/sc-auggie-review-protocol/SKILL.md\",\n        \"src/superclaude/skills/sc-auggie-review-protocol/refs/auggie-prompts.md\",\n        \".dev/eval-workspaces/sc-auggie-review/iteration-3/VERIFICATION.md\"\n      ],\n      \"why\": \"The correct Auggie invocation and JSON extraction pipeline is documented in 3 places with slight variations: (1) SKILL.md lines 152-170 (the canonical 'how to invoke Auggie' block), (2) refs/auggie-prompts.md lines 990-995 (anti-patterns section), (3) .dev/eval-workspaces/sc-auggie-review/iteration-3/VERIFICATION.md (empirical verification). The SKILL.md line 166 example omits the tail -n +2 step that line 167 says is mandatory when --max-turns is passed. This creates a 'read the whole block' dependency: a reader who copies the line 166 example without reading line 167 will encounter jq failures. The refs/auggie-prompts.md anti-patterns section correctly warns about the pitfall but doesn't provide the full corrected pipeline. The iteration-3 verification doc has the correct full pipeline but it's buried in an eval workspace, not surfaced in the skill.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Consolidate the Auggie invocation documentation into a single refs/auggie-cli-usage.md file with: (1) the full invocation recipe (including --max-turns preamble handling), (2) step-by-step JSON extraction pipeline with inline comments, (3) common pitfalls as a checklist. Reference this file from SKILL.md Wave 2 and from refs/auggie-prompts.md. Update SKILL.md line 166 to either include the full pipeline or add a forward reference: 'See refs/auggie-cli-usage.md for the complete extraction pipeline when --max-turns is used.'\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes_for_orchestrator\": \"Reviewed 11 files (1370-line diff) across 6 focus areas. Security findings are medium-severity (hook input handling, XML interpolation) — no critical exploits. Highest-signal findings: (1) matcher 'Bash' performance issue (high — fires on every Bash call), (2) install_hooks.py drift between project-local vs global scripts (high — creates unused copies), (3) evals.json lacking assertions (high — no automated regression coverage for a 362-line complex skill). Architecture and testing gaps are cross-cutting. All findings cite real file:line. Confidence is high for findings grounded in diff inspection + codebase cross-reference; medium for findings requiring runtime behavior assumptions (e.g., jq availability, hook firing frequency).\"\n}\n```\n","is_error":false,"subtype":"success","session_id":"13958576-73c9-4031-b96c-4970786d4444","num_turns":0,"request_id":"b20ccef8-15bf-4429-8984-ffa3606753ed"}
